    "body": "## Summary\nFix sgl-project/sglang#8540.\n\nAdds a per-request image-count bound across the multimodal processor\npipeline.  Each 4K image costs roughly 1 GiB GPU memory with the fast\nimage processor, so unbounded multi-image requests can easily OOM the\nserving instance.\n\n### Changes\n\nThree layers of validation to fail fast before any heavy image preprocessing:\n\n1. **Rust ingress prefetch** (`config.py`): the default\n   `{\"image\": 5}` is propagated to the Rust side so early requests can be\n   rejected there too.\n2. **Python TokenizerManager** (`tokenizer_manager.py`):\n   `_validate_mm_limits()` now falls back to\n   `BaseMultimodalProcessor.DEFAULT_IMAGE_NUM_LIMITATION = 5` instead of\n   skipping validation when no limit is configured.\n3. **BaseMultimodalProcessor** (`base_processor.py`): a defensive check in\n   `validate_mm_data()` that honours the ServerArg override if set, or the\n   class-level constant otherwise.\n\nOperators can tune the bound or disable it:\n\n```bash\n# default: 5 images\nsglang serve ...\n\n# custom bound\nsglang serve ... --limit-mm-data-per-request '{\"image\": 10}'\n\n# disable all limits\nsglang serve ... --limit-mm-data-per-request '{}'\n```\n\n## Test Plan\n- [x] Code inspection: validation runs before preprocess in all 3 layers\n- [ ] Covered by CI\n\n/cc @merrymercy\n\n---\nDCO: Signed-off-by: yancy <yancy@users.noreply.github.com>\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #38414303599](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38414303599)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38414304356](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38414304356)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38414304566](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38414304566)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states