  "issue_comments": [
    {
      "body": "@mickqian @JustinTong0323 @merrymercy @HaiShaw — Hi folks, #8540 asked for a per-request image-count bound to prevent OOM from 4K images (roughly 1 GiB each). This PR adds a default limit of 5 with override via the existing `--limit-mm-data-per-request` ServerArg. Validation runs at three layers — Rust ingress, Python TokenizerManager, BaseProcessor — so bad requests fail fast. 73/4 across 3 files. Mind taking a look? Thanks!\n",
      "created_at": "2026-10-13T14:34:03Z",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/pull/44078#issuecomment-6147976658",
      "id": 6147976658,
      "updated_at": "2026-10-13T14:34:03Z",
      "user": {
        "login": "Asthenia0412"
      }
